prompt:
You are a formal verification assistant. The following Dafny program fails Dafny verification.

=== PROGRAM ===
method BinarySearch(a: array<int>, key: int) returns (n: int)
    requires forall i, j :: 0 <= i < j < a.Length ==> a[i] <= a[j]
    ensures 0 <= n <= (a.Length) - 1
    ensures forall i :: 0 <= i < n ==> a[i] < key
    ensures forall i :: n <= i < a.Length ==> key <= a[i]
{
    var lo, hi := 0, a.Length;

    while lo < hi
        invariant 0 <= lo <= hi <= a.Length
        invariant forall i :: 0 <= i < lo ==> a[i] < key
        invariant forall i :: hi <= i < a.Length ==> key <= a[i]
    {
        var mid := (lo + hi) / 2;

        if a[mid] < key {
            lo := mid + 1;
        } else {
            hi := mid;
        }
    }

    n := lo;
}

=== DAFNY ERROR ===
program.dfy(6,0): Error: a postcondition could not be proved on this return path

program.dfy(3,19): Related location: this is the postcondition that could not be proved
  |
3 |     ensures 0 <= n <= (a.Length) - 1
  |                    ^^

Dafny program verifier finished with 1 verified, 1 error

=== COUNTEREXAMPLE ===
At initial state: a.Length = 1, key = 0. At a program state: hi = 1, lo = 0.

Analyze the failure and respond with ONLY a valid JSON object — no explanation, no markdown, no code fences. Use exactly this structure:

{
  "spec_element": "<one of: requires | invariant | ensures>",
  "proof_obligation": "<one of: initiation | preservation | bridge>",
  "diagnosis": "<explanation of what broke and why>",
  "repair": "<the corrected Dafny specification line that restores the intended behavior>"
}

Definitions:
- requires: the precondition that must hold before the method executes
- invariant: the loop invariant that must hold throughout the loop
- ensures: the postcondition that the method must guarantee on return
- initiation: the precondition does not establish the invariant at loop entry
- preservation: the loop body does not maintain the invariant
- bridge: the invariant and loop exit condition do not imply the postcondition

raw_response:
{
  "spec_element": "ensures",
  "proof_obligation": "bridge",
  "diagnosis": "The postcondition upper bound 'a.Length - 1' is too tight. The loop invariant allows lo to reach a.Length (when all elements are less than key, e.g., a.Length=1, key=0, a[0]<0, so lo becomes 1 = a.Length). At loop exit, lo == hi and 0 <= lo <= a.Length, so n = lo can legitimately equal a.Length. The bridge from the invariant-at-exit to the postcondition fails because n <= a.Length does not imply n <= a.Length - 1.",
  "repair": "ensures 0 <= n <= a.Length"
}
